       <li><strong>Local storage:</strong> keeps profile pairing, session tab bindings and a temporary save draft.</li>
       <li><strong>Alarms:</strong> attempts to reconnect a paired profile after the companion disconnects. It never retries an opening command automatically.</li>
       <li><strong>Optional access to a site:</strong> requested only when you choose to allow that site. It lets Workbench identify and focus its saved tabs. A new subdomain needs a new grant. Although Chrome describes this as site access, the extension uses tab addresses and does not inspect or change the page.</li>
+      <li><strong>Optional bookmarks:</strong> lets you search and open this profile’s existing bookmarks. Chrome’s permission can allow bookmark changes, but Workbench uses only read methods. You can revoke this permission in Chrome; subsequent searches and opens stop.</li>
